  Em seguida, calculamos \[\begin{aligned}
  \text{Var}(X) &=& E\left(X^2\right)-[E(X)]^2 = 4.17-(1.91)^2 = 0.522\\
  \text{Var}(Y) &=& E\left(Y^2\right)-[E(Y)]^2 = 2817-(51.3)^2 = 185.31
  \end{aligned}\]

