    \(0.602\)
  \item
    \(-2.922\)
  \item
    \(-0.398\)
  \item
    \(-0.279\)
  \item
    \(-2.045\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  Primeiramente devemos completar a tabela com as probabilidades
  marginais de \(X\) e \(Y\):

  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}cccc@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  X Y & 30 & 60 & P(X=x) \\
  \midrule\noalign{}
  \endhead
  \bottomrule\noalign{}
  \endlastfoot
  1 & 0.01 & 0.16 & 0.17 \\
  2 & 0.05 & 0.54 & 0.59 \\
  3 & 0.12 & 0.12 & 0.24 \\
  P(Y=y) & 0.18 & 0.82 & 1 \\
  \end{longtable}

  Em seguida, calculamos \[\begin{aligned}
  \text{Var}(X) &=& E\left(X^2\right)-[E(X)]^2 = 4.69-(2.07)^2 = 0.405\\
  \text{Var}(Y) &=& E\left(Y^2\right)-[E(Y)]^2 = 3114-(54.6)^2 = 132.84
  \end{aligned}\]

  A distribuição do produto é dada por

  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}cccccc@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  k & 30 & 60 & 90 & 120 & 180 \\
  \midrule\noalign{}
  \endhead
  \bottomrule\noalign{}
  \endlastfoot
  P(XY = k) & 0.01 & 0.21 & 0.12 & 0.54 & 0.12 \\
  \end{longtable}

  De modo que
  \[E(XY) = 30\times0.01+60\times0.21+90\times0.12+120\times0.54+180\times0.12 = 110.1\]
  e, portanto,
  \[\text{Corr}(X,Y) = \frac{\text{Cov}(X,Y)}{\sqrt{\text{Var}(X)}\sqrt{\text{Var}(Y)}} = \frac{E(XY)-E(X)E(Y)}{\sqrt{\text{Var}(X)}\sqrt{\text{Var}(Y)}} = -0.398\]

